      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.5.01-01",
      "block_type": "definition",
      "heading": "Uses and competing demands",
      "text": "Water supports domestic needs, agriculture, industry and functioning ecosystems. Users may share the same river, aquifer, reservoir or distribution network, so decisions in one place can affect supply elsewhere. Competition becomes especially important where usable supply is limited or varies seasonally. A management explanation should identify the users, source, period and constraint rather than assume that the presence of water means every demand can be met.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-1",
