      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.5.01-02",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Agricultural uses include crop irrigation, livestock drinking and suitable cleaning or processing activities on farms. Crops also use rainwater stored in the soil. Irrigation is deliberate application rather than any water a plant receives. The amount needed depends on crop, weather, soil and management. In Namibia farming is the largest user: in 2008 irrigation took about 40% of national water demand and livestock 26%, compared with about 20% for towns and industry, 6% for tourism, 5% for mining and 3% for rural households.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-2",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-01-1",
