      "repair_note": "Claude cross-review repairs: 6137-2.5-001 002 003 004 005 006"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.5.01-03",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Domestic uses include drinking, cooking, washing, sanitation and cleaning. Adequate quantity and suitable quality both matter. A source may contain water that requires treatment before a particular use, while a safe supply can still be too distant or unreliable for practical access. A household connection count therefore does not describe all aspects of service. Availability when needed, affordability and the time required to obtain water influence its usefulness.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-2",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-01-2",
