    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.5.01-05",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Ecosystems also require water. River flows support aquatic habitats and connected wetlands, while groundwater can support springs or other ecological functions. Allocating the whole measured supply to immediate abstraction can damage these functions or reduce downstream access. A management account should therefore consider relevant environmental needs as well as the three main human-use categories. The appropriate allocation depends on the actual resource and evidence, not an assumption that unused water has no value.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-2",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-01-2",
