    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.5.01-06",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Competition can occur between sectors or within one sector. A city and irrigation scheme may rely on the same reservoir, while upstream and downstream farmers may share a river. A new user can increase demand without increasing supply. Scarcity may be seasonal, spatial or linked to treatment and delivery capacity rather than a complete absence of water. Identify which stage creates the shortage before selecting a response.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-2",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-01-2",
