    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.5.01-07",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A hypothetical daily account illustrates the balance. Usable supply is 100 cubic metres; domestic need is fifty, agriculture forty and industry thirty. Combined need is 120, twenty above supply. Those demands cannot all be fully met from that stated supply during the interval without additional water, reduced demand or changed timing. The arithmetic does not establish which user should bear the gap; that is a management decision requiring priorities and consequences.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-2",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-01-2",
