    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.5.01-08",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A volume account must use consistent units and periods. One cubic metre equals 1,000 litres. A daily figure cannot be directly compared with a monthly total without a suitable conversion. Likewise, a reservoir's stored volume is not the same as the daily rate available through a treatment plant. The store might be substantial while pumping or treatment restricts delivery. An explanation should state whether it concerns stock, flow or service capacity.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-2",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-01-2",
