    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.5.01-09",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Conservation reduces avoidable use or loss while maintaining necessary services where possible. Repairing leaks, using suitable equipment, adjusting irrigation or reusing water can help. Their effects need measurement. Lower use per person does not establish a lower total if the population served increases sufficiently. A demand-management judgement should compare total withdrawal or delivery alongside the rate relevant to the service.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-2",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-01-1",
