    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.5.01-10",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Consider a household system serving 100 people at 100 litres per person per day: total use is 10,000 litres. If use falls to eighty litres per person while the number served rises to 150, total demand becomes 12,000 litres. The per-person improvement is real, but total demand is 2,000 litres higher. A manager needs both measures before deciding whether the scheme's capacity is adequate.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-1",
