    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.5.01-11",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Pricing and restrictions can influence demand, but effects depend on affordability, essential needs and people's ability to change practices. A higher charge may encourage reducing discretionary use while creating difficulties for low-income households if basic needs are not protected. A restriction announced without monitoring or workable alternatives may not achieve its aim. Judge actual access and savings rather than treating a policy statement as a delivered outcome.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-2",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-01-1",
