    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.5.01-12",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Allocation also has a time dimension. Storing water during a wetter period can support later use, while excessive current withdrawal can weaken drought reserves. Maintenance and quality protection help retain usable supply. Short-term receipts from one user should not be the sole criterion where households, livelihoods and ecosystems depend on continued availability. A useful decision explains whose needs are protected, what constraint remains and what evidence supports the balance.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-2",
