    },
    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.5.01-16",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A management proposal can also displace pressure. Supplying one district from a new source may reduce its local shortage while increasing abstraction in another catchment. The connection should be assessed through source sustainability, delivery needs and affected users. An inter-basin transfer changes where water is available but does not create water without costs or consequences. A map of the route is only part of the evidence needed for an overall judgement.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-2",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-01-2",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-02-1",
