    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.5.01-17",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Different responses operate at different timescales. Fixing a leaking connection can save part of a current delivery, while a new reservoir requires planning, construction and later filling. Emergency supply may protect immediate needs without being an affordable permanent system. The appropriate comparison should state whether the aim is today's access, next season's reserve or longer-term capacity. A measure can be useful for one aim without fully meeting the others.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-2",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-01-2",
        "CL-6137-2.5.01-02-1",
